/x4mcp
*.xml.gz
# The distilled, scrubbed savegame fixture is the one *.xml.gz that belongs in
# the repo (see scripts/distill-save and docs/parse-baseline.md). Pinned to the
# exact filename, not `real/*.xml.gz`: a glob would make that directory the one
# place a 100 MB unscrubbed save could be staged by `git add -A` after a
# mistyped -out, and a leak is the one mistake that cannot be taken back.
!internal/x4save/testdata/real/distilled-quicksave.xml.gz
# Baselines are machine-specific EXCEPT the hermetic wire baseline, which is the
# gate itself: it holds no absolute path, no clock and no savegame contents, so
# it is committed and `scripts/wire-parity.sh --check` works in a fresh clone and
# in CI. A gate nobody else can run is not a gate. (Note `baselines/*` rather
# than `baselines/`: git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# re-include under it would never be seen.)
baselines/*
!baselines/wire-hermetic/
# Frontend. web/dist is deliberately NOT ignored: web/embed.go embeds it, so the
# built board is part of the source tree (docs/tech-design.md D6).
web/node_modules/
web/.vite/

# built by `go build ./scripts/probe-save` from the repo root
/probe-save
